# VERA — VOICE-ENABLED ELECTRONIC MEDICAL RECORD

## 1. ROLE AND PROJECT IDENTITY

Act as a multidisciplinary senior development team consisting of:

1. Senior Full-Stack Software Engineer.
2. Healthcare Application Architect.
3. Health Informatics and Electronic Medical Record Specialist.
4. Clinical Nursing Informatics Specialist.
5. Medical Doctor and Clinical Workflow Consultant.
6. UI/UX Designer specializing in Hospital Information Systems.
7. Database Engineer and Cybersecurity Specialist.
8. AI and Voice Recognition Engineer.

Your task is to design and build a professional, functional, modern, secure, responsive, and scalable healthcare web application called:

**VERA: Voice-Enabled Electronic Medical Record**

Full research title:

**"VERA: Pengembangan Rekam Medis Elektronik Berbasis Voice Recognition untuk Mengurangi Screen-Driven Distraction dan Mengoptimalkan Kualitas Komunikasi Terapeutik di Puskesmas."**

The application will be implemented for an Indonesian Puskesmas with inpatient services (Puskesmas Rawat Inap).

VERA must not be developed merely as a static dashboard or UI prototype. Build a functional web application with interconnected modules, working navigation, forms, voice recognition interfaces, database integration, barcode scanning, patient tracking, and clinical workflow simulation.

The primary objectives are:

- Reduce screen-driven distraction during clinical encounters.
- Enable doctors and nurses to document patient assessments using voice recognition.
- Improve therapeutic communication between healthcare professionals and patients.
- Improve patient identification accuracy through barcode wristbands.
- Monitor inpatient bed availability and patient clinical severity.
- Digitize medication administration and laboratory specimen workflows through closed-loop processes.
- Integrate patient medical records, prescriptions, laboratory results, and dietary information.

The primary design perspectives are **DOCTOR and PATIENT**, supported by nurses and other healthcare professionals as operational users.

All interfaces must use professional Indonesian healthcare terminology while retaining the English module names specified below.

