# 25. FINAL PRODUCT VISION

VERA must represent a new approach to patient-centered clinical documentation.

It must connect three major dimensions:

**DIMENSION 1 — HUMAN-CENTERED CARE**

Doctors and nurses can devote more attention to the patient, maintain eye contact, listen actively, and communicate therapeutically while documenting clinical information through voice recognition.

**DIMENSION 2 — INTELLIGENT ELECTRONIC MEDICAL RECORD**

All patient assessments, clinical progress notes, prescriptions, laboratory results, and nursing interventions are integrated into one structured medical record.

**DIMENSION 3 — CLOSED-LOOP PATIENT SAFETY**

Barcode-based patient identification connects the patient's wristband with medication administration, laboratory specimens, and dietary services to improve identification accuracy and traceability.

The ultimate objective is to create an integrated system that places the patient at the center of clinical care, minimizes unnecessary screen interaction, improves documentation efficiency, and supports safer inpatient services at Indonesian Puskesmas.

